    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p><em>Queen Ehlissa’s Marvelous Nightingale</em> is named for its first owner, a queen of the eastern Flanaess in the world of Greyhawk. Its origin is unknown, but one legend says it was made to console the queen after a beloved pet songbird met an unfortunate end.</p><p>This mechanical songbird has crystal eyes, golden feathers, and a small windup key on its back. As a Magic action, you can make it spring to life for 10 minutes, singing a beautiful melody that can be heard within 300 feet, or you can return it to its mechanical form. Once the nightingale becomes mechanical again, it can’t come to life again for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Ensemble Casting.</strong> The nightingale has 6 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. As a Bonus Action while it is singing within 60 feet of you, you can expend charges to cast one of the spells on the following table from it (save DC 18), expending the number of charges it shows.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charges</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCalmEmotio]{Calm Emotions}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCompulsion]{Compulsion}</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDelayedBla]{Delayed Blast Fireball}</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDetectEvil]{Detect Evil and Good}</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplGreaterRes]{Greater Restoration}</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPrismaticS]{Prismatic Spray}</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSlow000000]{Slow}</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSpeakwithA]{Speak with Animals}</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Aura of Truth.</strong> While the nightingale sings, the effect of a @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplZoneofTrut]{Zone of Truth} spell (save DC 18) fills a 15-foot Emanation originating from it. While attuned to the nightingale, you know which creatures succeed or fail on the saving throw against this effect.</p><p><strong>Counterspell.</strong> While the nightingale sings, you can take a Reaction to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCounterspe]{Counterspell} (save DC 18) in response to that spell’s trigger. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Artifact has the following random properties (see “Artifacts” in the <em>Dungeon Master’s Guide</em>):</p><ul><li><p>2 minor beneficial properties</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying the Nightingale.</strong> The nightingale is destroyed if it is released into a whirlwind in Limbo.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-vHRVTwEDbx1xuGHy\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. Après <em>Spring to Life</em>, le rossignol ne peut revenir à la vie pendant 1 heure une fois redevenu mécanique.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
